{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and the LORD did to Sarah as he had spoken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Sarah conceived and bore Abraham a son in his old age, at the set time of which God had spoken to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham called the name of his son that was born to him, whom Sarah bore to him, Isaac.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham circumcised his son Isaac, being eight days old, as God had commanded him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham was a hundred years old, when his son Isaac was born to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Sarah said, God hath made me to laugh, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all that hear will laugh with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she said, Who would have said to Abraham, that Sarah shall nurse children? for I have borne him a son in his old age.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the child grew, and was weaned: and Abraham made a great feast the day that Isaac was weaned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Sarah saw the son of Hagar the Egyptian, which she had borne to Abraham, mocking.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, she said to Abraham, Cast out this bond-woman, and her son: for the son of this bond-woman shall not be heir with my son, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with Isaac.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the thing was very grievous in Abraham's sight, because of his son.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God said to Abraham, Let it not be grievous in thy sight, because of the lad, and because of thy bond-woman; in all that Sarah hath said to thee, hearken to her voice: for in Isaac shall thy seed be called.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And also of the son of the bond-woman will I make a nation, because he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy seed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham rose early in the morning, and took bread, and a bottle of water, and gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Hagar (putting ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on her shoulder) and the child, and sent her away; and she departed, and wandered in the wilderness of Beer-sheba.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the water was spent in the bottle, and she cast the child under one of the shrubs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she went, and sat her down over against ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", a good way off, as it were a bow-shot: for she said, Let me not see the death of the child. And she sat over against ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and raised her voice, and wept.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God heard the voice of the lad: and the angel of God called to Hagar out of heaven, and said to her, What aileth thee, Hagar? fear not; for God hath heard the voice of the lad where he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, lift up the lad, and hold him in thy hand: for I will make him a great nation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of water: and she went, and filled the bottle with water, and gave the lad drink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God was with the lad; and he grew, and dwelt in the wilderness, and became an archer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he dwelt in the wilderness of Paran: and his mother took for him a wife out of the land of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass at that time, that Abimelech, and Phichol the chief captain of his host, spoke to Abraham, saying, God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee in all that thou doest:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore swear to me here by God, that thou wilt not deal falsely with me, nor with my son, nor with my son's son: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " according to the kindness that I have done to thee, thou shalt do to me, and to the land in which thou hast sojourned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham said, I will swear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham reproved Abimelech, because of a well of water, which Abimelech's servants had violently taken away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abimelech said, I know not who hath done this thing: neither didst thou tell me, neither yet have I heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but to-day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham took sheep and oxen, and gave them to Abimelech: and both of them made a covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham set seven ewe-lambs of the flock by themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abimelech said to Abraham, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mean",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " these seven ewe-lambs, which thou hast set by themselves?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seven ewe-lambs shalt thou take from my hand, that they may be a witness to me, that I have digged this well.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore he called that place Beer-sheba: because there they swore both of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus they made a covenant at Beer-sheba: Then Abimelech arose, and Phichol the chief captain of his host, and they returned into the land of the Philistines.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Abraham",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " planted a grove in Beer-sheba, and called there on the name of the LORD, the everlasting God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.21.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.21.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abraham sojourned in the land of the Philistines many days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
